                                      SUPPORT

            As a C-Index customer you will receive one year of
            Maintenance Support.  This includes free telephone support
            for resolving problems of the system not performing
            according to specification.  In addition, any assistance
            required for porting C-Index to new environments is provided
            at no charge.  In the event that you require assistance with
            designing or debugging your application, this service is
            provided on a consulting basis, charged at $60 per hour plus
            expenses.

            Trio Systems offers a full range of consulting services.  We
            can assist your development staff with helpful techniques
            for using C-Index.  We can also develop complete software
            products for retail distribution or in-house use.

                                 QUANTITY DISCOUNTS

            Trio Systems offers a quantity discount for multiple copies
            of C-Index used at a single site.  This discount schedule
            offers significant savings over the cost of supplying each
            programmer at the individual license price.  If you are
            interested, please contact us for more details.


                                     CODE SIZE

            The size of the C-Index code will vary depending on the
            compiler, the memory model being used, and how many C-Index
            functions are used by your application.

            For example, the C-Index code size for the Borland C++
            compiler using the large memory model is about 35K. This is
            for the code only, static memory usage is separate and
            depends on the number of buffers specified in the CINDEX.H
            header file.  As supplied, about 12K of static memory is
            used (10K for buffers, 2K for additional internal memory).


                                  PORTING C-INDEX

            C-Index/II is designed to be ported to any operating system
            with a K&R or ANSI C compiler.  Test utilities are supplied
            to verify that your port is working.  Special design
            considerations allow flexibility for unusual environments,
            such VAX/VMS and Mainframe systems, without requiring major
            code modifications.

            C-Index/PC is designed to work with any compiler or
            operating system running on an Intel architecture computer.
            Support is provided for Borland C running under MSDOS.



